  ---
  Setup Tab — What Each Feature Does

  1. Accelerometer Calibration ✅ (Implemented, MP-aligned)

  What it's for: The FC's accelerometer drifts from factory defaults over time, or the board isn't
  mounted perfectly level. This re-teaches the FC what "level" feels like in all 6 orientations
  (Level, Left, Right, Nose Down, Nose Up, Upside Down).

  How MP does it: Sends PREFLIGHT_CALIBRATION with param5=1. The FC sends back
  COMMAND_LONG(42429=ACCELCAL_VEHICLE_POS, param1=1..6) to tell the GCS which position to hold
  next. GCS replies with the same command to confirm. Ends on STATUSTEXT containing "calibration
  successful".

  What we provide: Matches MP exactly. FC-driven position sequencing (not local counter), confirms
  each position by sending ACCELCAL_VEHICLE_POS(42429) back, monitors STATUSTEXT for
  completion/failure. Has the 6-position visual grid with active/done states.

  Gap: None on the core protocol. MP also has a "Level only" button (param5=2) and "Simple accel"
  button (param5=4) — we only have the full 6-position cal.

  ---
  2. Compass Calibration ✅ (Implemented, MP-aligned)
  
  What it's for: Compensates for magnetic interference from the drone's electronics and motors on
  the compass readings. Must be done outdoors away from metal objects.

  How MP does it: Sends DO_START_MAG_CAL (42424) with param2=1 (retry on fail), param3=1 (autosave
  offsets to flash). Monitors MAG_CAL_PROGRESS and MAG_CAL_REPORT messages per compass ID. Cancel
  sends DO_CANCEL_MAG_CAL (42426). Requires reboot after success to apply new offsets.

  What we provide: Matches MP exactly. Sends DO_START_MAG_CAL with retry+autosave flags, groups
  progress by compass ID, shows per-compass progress bars and fitness score, cancel sends
  DO_CANCEL_MAG_CAL, and shows a reboot prompt on completion.

  Gap: None critical.

  ---
  3. Motor Test ✅ (Implemented)
  
  What it's for: Spins individual motors to verify correct rotation direction and ESC response
  before flight. Also tests that motor numbering matches ArduPilot's expected layout.

  How MP does it: Sends DO_MOTOR_TEST (209) with param1=motor_number (1-based), param2=0 (throttle
  type = percent), param3=throttle_pct, param4=duration_s. Motor 0 = stop all.

  What we provide: Sends DO_MOTOR_TEST per motor (1-8), configurable throttle (5-30%) and duration.
   Stop-all bypasses command queue and fires raw zero-throttle commands directly to motors 1-8
  (matching MP's stopMotors()). Throttle capped at 30% as a safety limit.

  Gap: MP also has CompassMot (compass interference calibration) — a completely different feature
  where you spin all motors at increasing throttle while the system records COMPASSMOT_STATUS
  packets showing interference % vs. current. This is separate from motor test and we don't have
  it. We could add a "CompassMot" sub-tab if needed.

  ---
  4. Battery Monitor ✅ (Partial — core implemented)
  
  What it's for: Tells the FC how to measure battery voltage and current — which pins the sensing
  hardware is connected to, the voltage divider ratio, and amperes-per-volt scaling. Wrong
  calibration → wrong voltage/current readings → bad failsafe triggering.

  How MP does it: Reads/writes BATT_MONITOR, BATT_CAPACITY, BATT_VOLT_MULT, BATT_AMP_PERVLT,
  BATT_VOLT_PIN, BATT_CURR_PIN. Has hardware board presets (Pixhawk/Cube/APM → auto-fills the right
   pin numbers). Has sensor presets (Attopilot 45A/90A/180A, 3DR Power Module → auto-fills
  VOLT_MULT and AMP_PERVLT). Has a "measured voltage calibration" wizard: enter your multimeter
  reading → computes new multiplier.

  What we provide: Reads/writes the core params (BATT_MONITOR, BATT_CAPACITY, BATT_VOLT_MULT,
  BATT_AMP_PERVLT, BATT_VOLT_PIN, BATT_CURR_PIN) plus failsafe thresholds (BATT_LOW_VOLT,
  BATT_CRT_VOLT, BATT_LOW_MAH). Shows live voltage/current/% from telemetry.

  Gaps:
  - No hardware board presets (Pixhawk/Cube → auto-fill pins)
  - No sensor presets (Attopilot → auto-fill multipliers)
  - No calibration wizard (enter multimeter reading → recalculate multiplier)
  - No BATT2_* support (second battery entirely absent)

  ---
  5. Flight Modes ✅ (Partial — core implemented)
  
  What it's for: Maps the 6 positions of your RC mode switch to 6 flight modes (e.g. Stabilize,
  AltHold, Loiter, Auto, RTL, Guided). The FC reads which mode to use from the RC PWM value on the
  designated channel.

  How MP does it: Reads FLTMODE1-6 params. Reads live PWM of the mode channel (FLTMODE_CH).
  Highlights which dropdown is currently active based on PWM thresholds: <1230=slot0,
  1231-1360=slot1, 1361-1490=slot2, 1491-1620=slot3, 1621-1749=slot4, ≥1750=slot5. Has Simple Mode
  (SIMPLE bitmask) and Super-Simple Mode (SUPER_SIMPLE bitmask) checkboxes per slot.

  What we provide: Reads/writes FLTMODE1-6, shows which mode is currently active as a "CURRENT"
  badge matching the telemetry mode string.

  Gaps:
  - No live RC PWM readout showing which slot is actually selected by stick position
  - No SIMPLE/SUPER_SIMPLE mode bitmask checkboxes per slot
  - No RC channel selector (FLTMODE_CH param)

  ---
  6. Failsafe Config ✅ (Partial — core implemented)
  
  What it's for: Defines what the FC does if it loses RC signal (throttle failsafe), battery gets
  critically low, or GCS telemetry link drops. Wrong settings → no failsafe action on signal loss,
  or constant false triggers.

  How MP does it: FS_THR_ENABLE + FS_THR_VALUE (PWM threshold — shows live ch3 PWM colored red if
  below threshold). FS_BATT_ENABLE/BATT_FS_LOW_ACT, FS_BATT_VOLTAGE, FS_BATT_MAH, BATT_LOW_TIMER.
  FS_GCS_ENABLE. Shows live armed status and GPS lock.

  What we provide: FS_BATT_ENABLE, FS_BATT_VOLTAGE, FS_BATT_MAH, FS_RC_ENABLE, FS_GCS_ENABLE,
  FS_EKF_ACTION, FS_EKF_THRESH, RTL_ALT, LAND_SPEED.

  Gaps:
  - FS_THR_VALUE is missing — this is the actual PWM threshold for RC loss detection (critical:
  without it, the FC uses whatever was last set) 
  - No live ch3 PWM vs threshold visual indicator
  - No BATT_LOW_TIMER (hysteresis: how many seconds battery must be low before triggering)
  - Firmware-aware param fallback missing (BATT_FS_LOW_ACT is the newer param, older firmware used
  FS_BATT_ENABLE)

  ---
  7. Radio Calibration ✅ (Implemented)
  
  What it's for: Records the min/max PWM range of each RC channel as you move all sticks to
  extremes. Without this, the FC doesn't know the full travel range of your transmitter and stick
  inputs will be incorrectly scaled.

  How MP does it: PREFLIGHT_CALIBRATION with param4=1. Monitors RC_CHANNELS messages, records live
  min/max per channel as sticks move. Writes RC1_MIN, RC1_MAX, RC1_TRIM (and same for RC2-RC8) when
   done.

  What we provide: Same flow — sends PREFLIGHT_CALIBRATION(param4=1), polls RC_CHANNELS or
  RC_CHANNELS_RAW for live PWM, records min/max per channel, shows a visual bar for each channel.
  Writes trim/min/max params on completion.

  Gap: None critical.

