  // params error solved :

   Status: All Errors Fixed, All Features Implemented
  
  Error 1 Fixed: ReferenceError: Cannot access 'paramMeta' before initialization

  Root cause: paramMeta was declared on line 24 but referenced inside a Zustand selector on line 9
  — a JavaScript Temporal Dead Zone violation (const is not accessible before its declaration
  line).

  Fix: Moved paramMeta and favorites useState declarations to the top of the component, before any
  hooks that use them.

  ---
  Error 2 Fixed: Warning: The result of getSnapshot should be cached

  Root cause: Two separate issues:
  1. The selector (state) => selectGroupedParameters(state, paramMeta, favorites) was an inline 
  closure that created a new array on every call. Zustand v5 uses React's useSyncExternalStore
  which requires a stable snapshot — a new array each render causes an infinite re-render loop.
  2. selectParameterSyncState returns { ... } — a new object literal on every call, same
  infinite-loop risk.
  
  Fix: Three-part solution:
  - Created a stable module-level selectRawParameters selector (outside the component, so its
  reference never changes)
  - Computed paramEntriesRaw using useMemo in the component body, depending on rawParameters and
  paramMeta
  - Wrapped selectParameterSyncState with useShallow from zustand/react/shallow so the returned
  object is shallow-compared instead of reference-compared

