  // blank page solved : 

   Fixed MapEditor.jsx:87 by wrapping selectMapVehicle with useShallow from zustand/react/shallow.

  Why this fixes it: selectMapVehicle (mapSelectors.js:11) builds a fresh { position, heading, 
  home, isStale, ... } object on every call. Zustand v5 uses useSyncExternalStore, which compares
  snapshots by reference — a new object every render means the snapshot is never "equal", React
  keeps re-rendering, and you hit the warning followed by the Maximum update depth exceeded crash.
  useShallow swaps in shallow-key equality, so the hook only re-renders when one of the field
  values actually changes. Same pattern already used in Params.jsx:36.


